---
// About page. Opens with the personal origin, pivots to the academic and
// analytical foundation, then frames the founder experience as the reason
// for a path into venture, consulting, and data science.
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { credentials } from "@/data/profile";
---

<Base title="About">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-10 pt-20">
    <h1 class="reveal font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      About
    </h1>
    <div
      class="reveal mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft dark:text-paper/80"
      style="transition-delay: 80ms"
    >
      <p>
        I was born in Monrovia, Liberia, and most of my family still lives there.
        Most clinics in the country run on paper records, and I watched files get
        misplaced, water damaged, or lost between visits. Seeing how much a system can
        shape who gets care is what first pulled me toward technology and the decisions
        behind it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That pull turned into a foundation at the University of Maryland. I earned a
        B.S. in Information Science and I am finishing a Master of Information Management,
        both at College Park. The training runs across the full stack of working with
        information, from data science and analytics to research methods and human
        centered design. It taught me to start from evidence, structure a messy problem,
        and turn analysis into a decision someone can act on.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also wanted to understand how things actually get built, so I cofounded
        <strong class="text-ink dark:text-paper">Frontground</strong>, a mobile first
        EMR for low resource clinics. I raised $25K, ran more than 60 physician
        interviews, and learned how an operator weighs a market, a team, and a roadmap
        under real constraints. That experience is the reason I am drawn to venture,
        consulting, and data science. Having sat in the founder seat, I read companies
        and problems from the inside, which is exactly the judgment those roles reward.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I work across three modes. I evaluate startups as a
        <strong class="text-ink dark:text-paper">Venture Fellow</strong> at the USM
        Maryland Momentum Fund, I build data products like
        <strong class="text-ink dark:text-paper">Ovara</strong> and
        <strong class="text-ink dark:text-paper">Kairo Health</strong>, and I keep using
        research to make sure the work points at a real problem. Healthcare access stays
        the value underneath it, but the throughline is broader. I want to evaluate and
        build at the intersection of data, technology, and the decisions that move them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
    <h2 class="reveal mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold">Education</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="reveal border-l-2 border-accent/40 pl-4">
        <div class="font-semibold">Master of Information Management</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-ink-muted dark:text-paper/55">
          University of Maryland, College Park. Expected 2027.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal border-l-2 border-accent/40 pl-4" style="transition-delay: 50ms">
        <div class="font-semibold">B.S. Information Science</div>
        <div class="text-sm text-ink-muted dark:text-paper/55">
          University of Maryland, College Park. 2024.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10">
    <h2 class="reveal mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold">Credentials</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      {
        credentials.map((credential, index) => (
          <div
            class="reveal border-l-2 border-accent/40 pl-4"
            style={`transition-delay: ${index * 50}ms`}
          >
            <div class="font-semibold">{credential.name}</div>
            <div class="text-sm text-ink-muted dark:text-paper/55">
              {credential.detail}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>